WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
An acorn grows into an oak.

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.970
A knife is made to cut.

3
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:10.040
Aristotle called this a thing's
telos: its end, or purpose.

4
00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.100
A thing is good when it fulfils its telos.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.770
Then what is a human being for?

6
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:21.500
Thomas Aquinas added a Christian belief:
God created everything with a purpose.

7
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:26.700
If humans are made for a purpose, can
reason alone work out how we should live?

8
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.470
In this mission, you'll climb
Aquinas' four tiers of law,

9
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.630
from eternal law down
to the laws of nations.

10
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.550
Then you'll trace one first principle
as it branches into rules for life.

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.230
Your mission: find out whether reason
alone can work out how we should live.
